## 1. Executive Summary

This report presents an empirical, end-to-end evaluation of the proposed **SPIKE-ATTENTION** (Spatio-Temporal Attention Spiking Neural Network, `st_snn`) against classical machine learning (`svm`) and deep neural network baselines (`cnn`, `rnn`, `plain_snn`) for five-class arrhythmia classification on two-channel ambulatory ECG.

Evaluation uses patient-grouped train, validation and held-out fold partitions. Validation metrics support early stopping; test metrics are reported only after fitting. Statistical observations are patient groups. Cross-validation fold test sets are held-out within each fold; their pooled out-of-fold predictions are not an independent external test set. No superiority claim is made without multiplicity-adjusted evidence.

